title: Proposed Forge worker and main-thread ownership
---
flowchart TB
    subgraph Browser["Browser execution contexts"]
        Main["Main JS thread<br/>Capture actions and render Canvas or DOM"]
        ViewBridge(["Actions and frame time to Rust<br/>Committed views to JS"])
        Runtime["Rust main thread<br/>Own game state, fixed ticks and replay<br/>Verify digests and validate assets"]
        Effects(["Typed I/O requests to JS<br/>Correlated results to Rust"])
        IO["JS I/O workers<br/>Fetch bounded bytes and deliver results"]
        Main <--> ViewBridge <--> Runtime
        Runtime <--> Effects <--> IO
        IO -. Relay committed views .-> Main
    end
    subgraph Services[" "]
        Host["Future Studio milestone<br/>Forge host admits commands and queues builds"]
        Queue["PostgreSQL<br/>Persist Studio jobs, leases and events"]
        Builder["Native Studio build worker<br/>Claim leases and execute pinned builds<br/>Resolve worker-scoped providers"]
        Artifacts["Artifact store<br/>Immutable bytes by digest"]
        Host <--> Queue
        Queue <--> Builder
        Builder --> Artifacts
    end
    IO <--> Host
